  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOBiM5Uc7-BOy-",
    "databaseId": 4261735614,
    "number": 3220,
    "title": "Zero controller update rate might trigger undefined behavior",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros-controls/ros2_control/issues/3220",
    "body": "https://github.com/ros-controls/ros2_control/blob/bb07fdd55a59ea750f06bb2fee7a3a1c113b10dd/controller_manager/src/controller_manager.cpp#L1606\n\nIf a user creates a controller with update rate equals to zero, the line above is undefined behavior according to the C++ docs. Modulo operator with 0 should not be used. Maybe there should be a check of the controller update rate before using it.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"></p><div class=\"Box Box--condensed my-2\">\n  <div class=\"Box-header f6\">\n    <p class=\"mb-0 text-bold\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/ros-controls/ros2_control/blob/bb07fdd55a59ea750f06bb2fee7a3a1c113b10dd/controller_manager/src/controller_manager.cpp#L1606\">ros2_control/controller_manager/src/controller_manager.cpp</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"mb-0 color-fg-muted\">\n         Line 1606\n      in\n      <a data-pjax=\"true\" class=\"commit-tease-sha Link--inTextBlock\" href=\"/ros-controls/ros2_control/commit/bb07fdd55a59ea750f06bb2fee7a3a1c113b10dd\">bb07fdd</a>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div itemprop=\"text\" class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper blob-wrapper-embedded data\">\n    <table class=\"highlight tab-size mb-0 js-file-line-container\" data-tab-size=\"8\" data-paste-markdown-skip=\"\">\n\n        <tbody><tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L1606\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"1606\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC1606\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-k\">else</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> (cm_update_rate % controller_update_rate != <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>) </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody></table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<p></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If a user creates a controller with update rate equals to zero, the line above is undefined behavior according to the C++ docs. Modulo operator with 0 should not be used. Maybe there should be a check of the controller update rate before using it.</p>",
